From 35132c911aaa1982eafbb22b7416faeae9d339ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:44:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refuse a pin to a held machine; never drop
 runs_on on a courier create [daveey]

Two ways a machine pin was accepted and then not honoured (card t_01a1c8e051c4b598, 2026-11-11).

1. Held machine. worker-1 was on Board hold from 02:17 to 05:19 UTC for an AZ migration. At 03:42 a MacBook
   kanban_create(placement="worker-1") returned ok with runs_on=[machine:worker-1]. A held machine's pickup
   imports nothing (eligible() -> "held") and the Board refuses its leases, so the card sat ready 48 min while the
   origin read "waiting for worker-1 ... queued, not stuck". placement_runs_on() and check_machine_pins() checked
   state and pickup, never hold.
   - check_machine_pins refuses a held machine (placement_unavailable, rejection machine_held, naming the unheld
     machines that pick up). The placement= path now runs the same check (kanban_sync_runstate.placement_runs_on),
     so tool placement=, tool runs_on= and `hermes kanban create --runs-on` all refuse (kanban move already
     refused a held target as no_machine).
   - A card already waiting when the hold lands: the queue place carries `held`, and the card read says ON HOLD
     and how to re-place it instead of "queued, not stuck".

2. runs_on on a courier create. kanban_create(placement="hub", runs_on=["machine:worker-1"]) created the card on
   the hub with runs_on NULL: hermes-hub create-task has no runs_on option, and runs_on was in neither
   CARRIED_OPTIONS nor UNCARRIED_OPTIONS. It is now uncarried: with a pin to another gateway the create is
   refused; without one the card stays on its board, where the Board lease reads the labels. An explicit []
   counts too.

Tests fail on main before this change (10) and pass after: test_kanban_held_machine_pin.py,
test_kanban_placement_runs_on.py, two new cases in test_kanban_placement.py.

test_every_create_parameter_is_classified_for_the_courier guards the cause of 2: a kanban_create parameter in
neither option list (nor the reviewed handled-elsewhere set) fails the test instead of being dropped.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_placement.py                |   8 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_queue_position.py           |  13 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_runstate.py            |  11 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_worker_node.py              |  36 +++++-
 .../test_kanban_held_machine_pin.py           | 121 ++++++++++++++++++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement.py     |   3 +
 .../test_kanban_placement_runs_on.py          |  65 ++++++++++
 7 files changed, 250 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_held_machine_pin.py
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement_runs_on.py

